> API and interpretation

Edges are undirected; duplicates add weight and self-loops are ignored after
endpoint validation. Empty input is a converged empty layout; singleton centers
to the origin, and the two-vertex legacy fallback repeats the second mode on
both axes. Run/trace expose unresolved cap outcomes. The legacy positions-only
API throws on nonconvergence. Approximate eigenvector signs and degenerate
subspaces must be compared through residuals/projectors rather than exact
coordinate bytes.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Hall (1970), An r-Dimensional Quadratic Placement Algorithm|https://doi.org/10.1287/mnsc.17.3.219]

